                <head>114. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The meeting of the Ministerial Council of the Organization for Economic
                    Cooperation and Development was held in Paris November 25–26, 1965. Under
                    Secretary of State for Economic Affairs Thomas C.
                        Mann headed the U.S. Delegation, which included AID Administrator David
                        E. Bell and Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs
                        Anthony M. Solomon. For a full list
                    of the U.S. Delegation, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, December 27, 1965, page 1039. Text of the communique,
                    November 26, is ibid., pages 1038–1039. Documentation on the meeting is in
                    Washington National Records Center, RG 286, DAC
                    Material: FRC 70 A 5922, Meetings—OECD Ministerial Meeting November 25–26, 1965; and
                    Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 66 D
                    347, CF 2564–2565.</p>
            </div>
